  49:     - Non-background cells form a regular grid of solid rectangular sprite slots, plus sparse stray foreground noise.
  50:     - Every slot contains a corrupted copy of the same sprite, preserving non-background occupancy.
  51: 
  52:     Rule
  53:     - Find the dense row bands and dense column bands of the slot array.
  54:     - For each relative position inside the sprite rectangle, take the unique majority color across all slots.
  55:     - Fill every slot with that recovered sprite and set all other cells to background.
  56: 
  57:     Key insight
  58:     - The intended sprite support is the Cartesian product of dense row bands and dense column bands; noise is too sparse to enter the high-density bands consistently.
  59:     """
